WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.997
Pause in a position that is safe and supported.

2
00:00:06.697 --> 00:00:11.194
Let the eyes stay open or close.

3
00:00:12.894 --> 00:00:17.394
Feel the feet, the seat, or the back meeting a surface.

4
00:00:21.488 --> 00:00:22.928
Notice the hands.

5
00:00:24.628 --> 00:00:29.357
Are they holding, pressing, or preparing to act?

6
00:00:31.057 --> 00:00:37.154
Without forcing them open, let each finger feel the surface beneath it.

7
00:00:38.854 --> 00:00:42.941
Allow the hands to have weight.

8
00:00:49.082 --> 00:00:51.042
Bring attention to the jaw.

9
00:00:52.742 --> 00:00:57.890
Notice the tongue and the space between the teeth.

10
00:00:59.590 --> 00:01:06.492
If it is comfortable, make one small movement of the jaw and let it find a resting position.

11
00:01:12.633 --> 00:01:13.993
Check the shoulders.

12
00:01:15.693 --> 00:01:22.215
Rather than pulling them down, feel where they connect to the arms and upper back.

13
00:01:23.915 --> 00:01:28.877
Ask whether they can be carried with slightly less effort.

14
00:01:36.553 --> 00:01:38.873
Take one ordinary breath.

15
00:01:40.573 --> 00:01:42.773
A clenched place may remain.

16
00:01:44.473 --> 00:01:56.942
Let the nearby body stay available too: face around the jaw, arms around the hands, chest beneath the shoulders.

17
00:02:04.618 --> 00:02:09.848
Notice whether the mind is gripping a sentence, plan, or demand.

18
00:02:11.548 --> 00:02:16.500
You do not have to discard it.

19
00:02:18.200 --> 00:02:22.342
For one breath, let it wait without being worked on.

20
00:02:30.018 --> 00:02:34.388
Feel hands, jaw, and shoulders together.

21
00:02:36.088 --> 00:02:40.720
Keep the effort you need and release only what is ready to go.

22
00:02:46.861 --> 00:02:51.488
Look around the room and make the next movement slowly.

23
00:02:53.188 --> 00:03:00.000
You can return to these three places whenever you need a brief check for unnecessary holding.
